 Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
 
+## Defects found
+
+Browser acceptance suite reports 10 failures, all from the same root cause: `render()` in `js/app.js` rebuilds the entire `<li>` list from scratch on every state change, causing:
+
+1. **DOM detachment** (4 failures): Toggle/toggle-all/destroy handlers call `render()`, which replaces all `<li>` nodes. Cypress references to pre-click elements become detached.
+
+2. **Editing state lost** (6 failures): The dblclick handler sets `todo.editing = true` on the in-memory object, then calls `render()`, which re-reads from localStorage (never updated with `editing`). The `editing` class is never applied to the `<li>`, so the `.edit` input stays `display: none` per `todomvc-app-css`.
+
+Fix: Mutate existing DOM nodes in place (toggle class, checkbox state) instead of calling `render()`.
+
+## Durable changes this cycle
+
+- `features/dom-identity.feature` (new): `@contract` source-level conformance checks that pin the DOM-identity requirement
+- `watchbill.json` (new): Watch targets for the conformance checks
+
