+Feature: DOM identity
+  As a user
+  I want todo items to keep their DOM identity when I interact with them
+  So that the app works correctly with browser automation
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Toggle completion mutates in place
+
+  @contract
+  Scenario: The toggle click handler does not rebuild the todo list
+    Given the app source at "js/app.js"
+    When I check the toggle checkbox click handler
+    Then the handler toggles the "completed" class on the existing list item
+    And the handler does not call render() or set innerHTML on the todo list
+
+  @contract
+  Scenario: The double-click handler does not rebuild the todo list
+    Given the app source at "js/app.js"
+    When I check the label double-click handler
+    Then the handler adds the "editing" class to the existing list item
+    And the handler does not call render() or set innerHTML on the todo list
+
+  @contract
+  Scenario: The destroy button handler does not rebuild the entire list
+    Given the app source at "js/app.js"
+    When I check the destroy button click handler
+    Then the handler removes the list item element directly
+    And the handler does not set innerHTML on the todo list
+
+  Rule: Editing state is managed on the existing DOM node
+
+  @contract
+  Scenario: Double-clicking the label does not lose editing state through render
+    Given the app source at "js/app.js"
+    When I check the label double-click handler
+    Then the handler adds the "editing" class to the existing list item before any re-render
+    And the handler does not re-read todo state from localStorage after setting editing
+
+  Rule: Toggle-all mutates in place
+
+  @contract
+  Scenario: The toggle-all handler does not rebuild the todo list
+    Given the app source at "js/app.js"
+    When I check the toggle-all click handler
+    Then the handler toggles the "completed" class on each existing list item
+    And the handler does not set innerHTML on the todo list
